  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAKSHAM - Family Health Accelerator: Maternal Newborn and Child Health Accelerator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  . .India contributes 20 percent of the world&apos;s child deaths, 10 percent of maternal deaths, and is the largest contributor to prematurity-related complications. This activity will contribute to the UN Sustainable Development Goals and is aligned with the Global Strategy of Ending Preventable Maternal Mortality. The program will enhance the capacity of the Government of India (GOI), private sector, and civil society to work together to improve health outcomes.   .With FY 2022 funding, SAKSHAM will work closely with national and state governments to provide targeted technical assistance to state health societies, while also demonstrating innovative models at the district level. The project will focus on building sustainable state-level capabilities for high impact maternal, newborn, and child health service provision through improved quality of care and innovations, and will ensure that these interventions are adapted and scaled by the government and sustained through national and state budget and human resource provisions. .With FY 2022 funds, activities will focus on: 1) using Living Labs and Human Centered Design approaches to set up hybrid learning models; 2) leveraging the Mobile Medical Unit model in the Assam tea gardens; 3) applying data analytics to optimize data platforms, dashboards, and supply chain software for evidence-based decision-making, 4) engaging the private sector, including local entrepreneurs, businesses, and private healthcare providers in rural/tribal areas; 5) harnessing innovations through an Impact Lab to advance promising technologies; and 6) implementing Behavior Change Communication using innovative strategies for demand generation for quality MNCH services.</narrative>
  </description>
